MLB Analytics App by Chris Jones v1.5


A command‑line application for running MLB team analytics, standings projections, free agent evaluations, and R² analysis with visualizations based on data from 2015-present day.

_____________________________________________________________________________________

📂 Folder Contents

mlb_analytics_app.py : Launcher script with interactive menu
single_team_simulator.py : Evaluates team WAR vs payroll
standings_projections.py : Runs full standings projections
free_agent_evaluator.py : Adds free agent to team projections
r2_analysis.py : Runs R² analysis with visualizations
trade_simulator.py : Trade simulator module
stuff_plus_calculator.py : Manual Stuff+ calculator
current_player_stuff_plus.py : Statcast-based Stuff+ calculator for MLB players
team_projected_26man.py : 26-man roster builder + FA recommendations
projected_mlb_team_data.csv : Projected WAR data for all teams
mlb_finance_data_1.csv : Historical finance/performance dataset
2026_freeagents.csv : Free agent list for 2026
README.rtf : App overview and instructions
Output files (e.g. jonesy_mlb_projected_standings.csv)
_____________________________________________________________________________________

⚙️ Requirements

	•	Python 3.9+ (tested with Python 3.11)
	•	Required packages: python3 -m pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib scipy seaborn pybaseball (copy and paste into terminal

https://www.python.org/downloads/ <— Python download link

— IMPORTANT

1. Place the mlbapp folder on your Desktop Path should be: ~/Desktop/mlbapp
2. Open a terminal and navigate to the folder: cd ~/Desktop/mlbapp
3. Run the launcher: python3 mlb_analytics_app_v1.5.py  
_____________________________________________________________________________________

Usage
